<div style="font-family: -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, sans-serif; color: #111; max-width: 620px;">
  <h2 style="margin-bottom: 4px;">ParcelX credits are running low</h2>
  <p style="color: #555; margin-top: 0;">Checked <%= @checked_at.in_time_zone("Asia/Kolkata").strftime("%d %b %Y, %-I:%M %p") %> IST</p>

  <div style="border: 1px solid #f0c2c2; background: #fdf2f2; border-radius: 8px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 16px 0;">
    <div style="font-size: 34px; font-weight: 700; color: #b42318;"><%= number_with_delimiter(@credits) %></div>
    <div style="color: #777; font-size: 13px;">credits remaining (alert threshold <%= number_with_delimiter(@threshold) %>)</div>
  </div>

  <p style="font-size: 14px; color: #333;">
    Address lookups on <strong>iq.parcelx.in/vega/address</strong> stop working once the balance hits zero,
    which silently breaks COD address autofill and the address fallback. Top up with ParcelX to avoid that.
  </p>

  <p style="font-size: 12px; color: #999; margin-top: 24px;">
    Sent daily while the balance stays below the threshold. Set PARCELX_CREDIT_ALERT_THRESHOLD to change it.
  </p>
</div>
